% The governing obligation: an unrecognised builtin is E_UNSUPPORTED_CONSTRUCT,
% never a skipped constraint. The catalogue is open -- a solver may declare
% support for additional predicates -- so a frontend meets unknown names as a
% matter of course, and skipping one drops a constraint: more solutions, and
% the answer looks like success.
var int: x;
constraint cumulative([1], [1], [1], x);
solve satisfy;
